/**

@page page_exahype2_blockstructured Block-structured patch operations

\tableofcontents

ExaHyPE 2 embeds a patch into every cell of Peano's adaptive Cartesian grid: a
@f$ k \times k @f$ or @f$ k \times k \times k @f$ block of degrees of freedom
plus an optional halo layer around it. The routines below operate on that
layout and are independent of the numerical scheme, so the finite-volume, the
Runge-Kutta DG and the ADER-DG solvers all assemble their kernels from them.

## Functionality

\li `exahype2/Enumeration.h` Lexicographic serialisation of the voxel indices
  within a patch overlap (halo layer). This defines the canonical ordering of
  halo data.
\li `exahype2/amr/AMRRoutines.h` Interpolation of coarse patch data onto
  embedded fine patches at resolution transitions, together with the matching
  restriction of fine data back onto the coarse patch. These are the
  inter-resolution transfer operators for adaptive mesh refinement.
\li `exahype2/amr/ChildDataStage.h` Collects the data of the children of one
  coarse cell or face until the sweep restricts it.
\li `exahype2/amr/MultiresolutionDetail.h` Relative representation error of an
  affine fit over one patch. exahype2::refineOnDetail() maps it onto a
  refinement command.
\li `exahype2/Curvi.h` Transformation between a Cartesian domain and a
  curvilinear one whose cells are connected the same way but are not
  equidistant.

To plot patch data, use the writers in `tarch::plotter` (the VTU, HDF5 and
NetCDF writers together with `tarch::plotter::TimeSeriesWriter` for the
snapshot/index handling).

*/
